    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d342">

                <pb facs="0631" n="613" xml:id="pg613"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">357.AA/3–1251: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in Indonesia
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-03-12T19:00:00-05:00">March 12, 1951—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>977. Usgoc 495. Reur 954<anchor n="1" xml:id="d342-f1"/> and 955 Dept concurs
                    your suggestion that UNCI formally solicit
                    Netherlands and Indonesian views concerning Comm. Dept’s position still as you
                    stated that we advocate formal early dissolution. Believe that Comm’s action
                    shld at this time be aimed at eliciting formal expression views of parties on
                    this matter in view pending solution KL and
                        ex-KNIL problems.</p>
                <p>Sent to AmEmbassy Djakarta priority niact 977;
                    repeated USUN New York 775, AmEmbassy The Hague
                    1033.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d342-f1" n="1" xml:id="d342-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 1226(Gocus 954) from Djakarta,
                    March 9, Ambassador Cochran reported that Mr. Beam had again reiterated to his
                    colleagues on the UNCI that the United States
                    still favored the complete dissolution of the UNCI at the earliest possible date because of Indonesia’s
                    opposition to its continuance (357.AA/3–951).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
